peaks and valleys of the spectrum. Good for timbre analysis.\n\n7. **Tonnetz Features:**  \n   Tonal centroid features capturing harmonic relations, often used in music/audio analysis.\n\n8. **Mel Spectrogram:**  \n   Energy distribution across Mel frequency bands. Captures spectral content like MFCCs but more detailed.\n\n9. **Tempogram:**  \n   Captures tempo-related information over time.\n\n**Aggregation:**  \n- For each feature, we compute both the **mean** and **standard deviation** across time frames to get fixed-length vectors.\n- All features are **concatenated** into a single 1D feature vector for the audio file.\n\n**Output:**  \n- A 1D NumPy array containing all aggregated features, ready for ML model input.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==========================================================\n# 🎵 AUDIO FEATURE EXTRACTION FUNCTION\n# ==========================================================\ndef extract_audio_features(audio_path, sr=22050, n_mfcc=30, n_mels=128):\n    \"\"\"\n    Extract a variety of audio features from a single file and return a fixed-length feature vector.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    - audio_path (str): Path to the audio file\n    - sr (int): Sampling rate for loading audio\n    - n_mfcc (int): Number of MFCCs to extract\n    - n_mels (int): Number of Mel bands for Mel-spectrogram\n    \n    Returns:\n    - feats (np.ndarray): 1D array of concatenated mean+std features\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # 1️⃣ Load audio\n    y, _ = librosa.load(audio_path, sr=sr)\n    \n    # 2️⃣ MFCC (Mel-Frequency Cepstral Coefficients)\n    mfcc = librosa.feature.mfcc(y=y, sr=sr, n_mfcc=n_mfcc)\n    \n    # 3️⃣ Delta MFCC (first derivative)\n    delta = librosa.feature.delta(mfcc)\n    \n    # 4️⃣ Delta-Delta MFCC (second derivative)\n    delta2 = librosa.feature.delta(mfcc, order=2)\n    \n    # 5️⃣ Chroma features (harmonic content)\n    chroma = librosa.feature.chroma_stft(y=y, sr=sr)\n    \n    # 6️⃣ Spectral contrast (timbre info)\n    contrast = librosa.feature.spectral_contrast(y=y, sr=sr)\n    \n    # 7️⃣ Tonnetz features (tonal/harmonic info)\n    tonnetz = librosa.feature.tonnetz(y=y, sr=sr)\n    \n    # 8️⃣ Mel-spectrogram (energy distribution in Mel bands)\n    mel = librosa.feature.melspectrogram(y=y, sr=sr, n_mels=n_mels)\n    \n    # 9️⃣ Tempogram (tempo-related features)\n    tempogram = librosa.feature.tempogram(y=y, sr=sr)\n    \n    # 🔹 Aggregate features: mean + std for each\n    feats = np.concatenate([\n        mfcc.mean(1), mfcc.std(1),\n        delta.mean(1), delta.std(1),\n        delta2.mean(1), delta2.std(1),\n        chroma.mean(1), chroma.std(1),\n        contrast.mean(1), contrast.std(1),\n        tonnetz.mean(1), tonnetz.std(1),\n        mel.mean(1), mel.std(1),\n        tempogram.mean(1), tempogram.std(1)\n    ])\n    \n    return feats\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-01-02T20:19:01.080910Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-01-02T20:19:01.081490Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-01-02T20:19:01.088577Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-01-02T20:19:01.081449Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-01-02T20:19:01.087852Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":87},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# 🎯 Load Embeddings for All Candidates\n\nThis function `load_embeddings` is designed to **load embeddings and optionally extract audio features** for all candidates in the dataset.\n\n**Step-by-step explanation:**\n\n1. **Iterate over candidate IDs** using `tqdm` to show progress.  \n2. **Check candidate folder existence** (`os.path.exists`) and skip if missing.  \n3. **Check for JSON embeddings**: `emb_cough.json` and `emb_vowel.json`. Skip candidate if either is missing.  \n4. **Load JSON data** and flatten into 1D NumPy arrays.  \n5. **Combine embeddings** by concatenating cough and vowel embeddings.  \n6. **Optional audio feature extraction**:\n   - Checks for `cough.wav` and `vowel.wav`.\n   - Uses `extract_audio_features` to extract MFCC, Chroma, Mel-spectrogram, etc.\n   - Concatenates these features to the JSON embeddings.\n7. **Store in dictionary** with `candidate_id` as the key.  \n8. **Error handling:** Any exceptions are skipped to avoid breaking the loop.  \n9. **End message:** Prints how many candidates’ embeddings were successfully loaded out of the total.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# =======================\n# LOAD EMBEDDINGS FOR ALL CANDIDATES\n# =======================\ndef load_embeddings(candidate_ids, files_path):\n    embeddings_dict = {}\n    \n    for cid in tqdm(candidate_ids, desc=\"Loading embeddings\"):\n        cdir = os.path.join(files_path, cid)\n        if not os.path.exists(cdir):\n            continue\n        \n        cough_path = os.path.join(cdir, \"emb_cough.json\")\n        vowel_path = os.path.join(cdir, \"emb_vowel.json\")\n        \n        if not (os.path.exists(cough_path) and os.path.exists(vowel_path)):\n            continue\n        \n        try:\n            with open(cough_path, 'r') as f:\n                cough_data = json.load(f)\n            with open(vowel_path, 'r') as f:\n                vowel_data = json.load(f)\n            \n            if not cough_data or not vowel_data:\n                continue\n            \n            cough_emb = np.array(cough_data[0]).flatten()\n            vowel_emb = np.array(vowel_data[0]).flatten()\n            \n            # Combine embeddings\n            combined_emb = np.concatenate([cough_emb, vowel_emb])\n            \n            # Extra: extract audio features from actual audio if available\n            # Example: SOUND_DIR/{cid}/{file}.wav (adjust as needed)\n            cough_audio_file = os.path.join(cdir, \"cough.wav\")\n            vowel_audio_file = os.path.join(cdir, \"vowel.wav\")\n            \n            feats_list = []\n            if os.path.exists(cough_audio_file):\n                feats_list.append(extract_audio_features(cough_audio_file))\n            if os.path.exists(vowel_audio_file):\n                \n                feats_list.append(extract_audio_features(vowel_audio_file))\n            \n            if feats_list:\n                audio_feats = np.concatenate(feats_list)\n                combined_emb = np.concatenate([combined_emb, audio_feats])\n            \n            embeddings_dict[cid] = combined_emb\n        \n        except:\n            continue\n    \n    print(f\"✅ Loaded embeddings for {len(embeddings_dict)}/{len(candidate_ids)} candidates\")\n    return embeddings_dict","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-01-02T20:19:01.089299Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-01-02T20:19:01.089560Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-01-02T20:19:01.106836Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-01-02T20:19:01.089532Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-01-02T20:19:01.106191Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":88},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# 🏗 Main Pipeline Overview\n\nThe `main()` function orchestrates the full data processing and model training pipeline for the respiratory sound dataset.  \n\n**Step-by-step explanation:**\n\n1. **Load CSV:** Reads the training CSV file and prints total candidates.  \n\n2. **Preprocess tabular data:**\n   - Categorical columns (`gender`, `tbContactHistory`, etc.) are **label-encoded**.  \n   - Missing values in tabular features are handled using **most frequent imputation**.  \n   - `X_tabular` contains the numeric representation of tabular features.\n\n3. **Load embeddings:**  \n   - Calls `load_embeddings` to load precomputed embeddings and optionally extract audio features.  \n   - Filters candidates with **complete embeddings** only.\n\n4. **Prepare labels:**  \n   - Encodes the `disease` column into numeric labels.  \n\n5. **Split dataset:**  \n   - Performs an **80/20 stratified split** for train/test sets.  \n   - Ensures tabular and audio features match the split.  \n\n6. **Combine features:**  \n   - Concatenates **tabular features + audio embeddings** for each candidate.  \n   - Scales all features using `StandardScaler`.\n\n7. **Compute class weights:**  \n   - Calculates weights inversely proportional to class frequencies for **imbalanced data**.\n\n8. **Train CatBoostClassifier:**  \n   - Uses 500 iterations, learning rate 0.02, depth 4, L2 regularization, subsampling, and class weights.  \n   - Trains the model on the combined tabular + audio feature set.\n\n**Output:**  \n- Trained `CatBoostClassifier` model ready for evaluation or prediction.\n\n# 📊 Extended Model Evaluation\n\nThis section evaluates the trained CatBoost model using multiple performance metrics and visualizations:\n\n1. **Training & Test Accuracy:**  \n   - Compute accuracy on both training and test sets to check for overfitting.\n\n2. **Classification Report:**  \n   - Displays **precision, recall, F1-score** for each class with support counts.\n\n3. **Confusion Matrix:**  \n   - Heatmap visualization showing correct vs misclassified predictions for each class.\n\n4. **Precision, Recall, F1 (Macro & Weighted):**  \n   - Macro: treats all classes equally.  \n   - Weighted: accounts for class imbalance.\n\n5. **Matthews Correlation Coefficient & Cohen’s Kappa:**  \n   - Advanced metrics for multi-class classification, considering class balance and agreement.\n\n6. **Log Loss:**  \n   - Measures the probability-based error, penalizing confident wrong predictions.\n\n7. **ROC-AUC (Multi-Class):**  \n   - Evaluates the model’s ability to discriminate each class.  \n   - Macro: average of per-class AUCs.  \n   - Weighted: accounts for class support.\n\n8. **ROC Curves (One-vs-Rest):**  \n   - Plots **False Positive Rate vs True Positive Rate** for each class.  \n   - Diagonal line indicates random performance; curves above the line are better.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ==========================================================\n# 🔹 MAIN PIPELINE\n# ==========================================================\ndef main():\n    # 1️⃣ Load CSV\n    df = pd.read_csv(TRAIN_PATH)\n    print(f\"Total candidates: {len(df)}\")\n    \n    # 2️⃣ Preprocess tabular features\n    categorical_cols = ['gender', 'tbContactHistory', 'wheezingHistory',\n                        'phlegmCough', 'familyAsthmaHistory',\n                        'feverHistory', 'coldPresent']\n    \n    df_encoded = df.copy()\n    for col in categorical_cols:\n        le = LabelEncoder()\n        df_encoded[col] = le.fit_transform(df_encoded[col].astype(str))\n    \n    # Drop ID and target to create tabular feature matrix\n    X_tabular = df_encoded.drop(['candidateID','disease'], axis=1).values\n    \n    # Handle missing values\n    imputer = SimpleImputer(strategy='most_frequent')\n    X_tabular = imputer.fit_transform(X_tabular)\n    \n    # 3️⃣ Load embeddings (audio + precomputed)\n    candidate_ids = df['candidateID'].tolist()\n    embeddings_dict = load_embeddings(candidate_ids, SOUND_DIR)\n    \n    # Filter only candidates with complete embeddings\n    complete_candidates = [cid for cid in candidate_ids if cid in embeddings_dict]\n    df_complete = df_encoded[df_encoded['candidateID'].isin(complete_candidates)].reset_index(drop=True)\n    \n    # Align tabular features to filtered candidates\n    X_tabular_complete = X_tabular[[df_encoded[df_encoded['candidateID']==cid].index[0] for cid in complete_candidates]]\n    \n    # Encode target variable\n    y = LabelEncoder().fit_transform(df_complete['disease'])\n    \n    # 4️⃣ Stratified train-test split (80/20)\n    train_idx, test_idx = train_test_split(\n        np.arange(len(complete_candidates)),\n        test_size=0.2,\n        stratify=y,\n        random_state=42\n    )\n    \n    train_cids = [complete_candidates[i] for i in train_idx]\n    test_cids = [complete_candidates[i] for i in test_idx]\n    \n    # Match embeddings with split\n    X_train_audio = np.array([embeddings_dict[cid] for cid in train_cids])\n    X_test_audio = np.array([embeddings_dict[cid] for cid in test_cids])\n    \n    # Tabular features for split\n    X_train_tabular = X_tabular_complete[train_idx]\n    X_test_tabular = X_tabular_complete[test_idx]\n    \n    # Target for split\n    y_train = y[train_idx]\n    y_test = y[test_idx]\n    \n    # 5️⃣ Combine tabular + audio features\n    X_train = np.concatenate([X_train_tabular, X_train_audio], axis=1)\n    X_test = np.concatenate([X_test_tabular, X_test_audio], axis=1)\n    \n    # Scale combined features\n    scaler = StandardScaler()\n    X_train = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)\n    X_test = scaler.transform(X_test)\n    \n    # 6️⃣ Compute class weights for imbalanced data\n    class_counts = Counter(y_train)\n    class_weights = {k: sum(class_counts.values())/(len(class_counts)*v) for k,v in class_counts.items()}\n    \n    # 7️⃣ Train CatBoostClassifier\n    model = CatBoostClassifier(\n        iterations=500,\n        learning_rate=0.02,\n        depth=4,\n        l2_leaf_reg=15,\n        bootstrap_type='Bernoulli',\n        subsample=0.8,\n        eval_metric='MultiClass',\n        random_seed=42,\n        class_weights=class_weights,\n        border_count=32,\n        colsample_bylevel=0.8,\n        min_data_in_leaf=5,\n        verbose=100\n    )\n    \n    # Train model\n    model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n    \n    # ✅ Confirmation message\n    print(\"✅ Model training completed successfully!\")\n    \n    # ==========================================================\n    # 🔹 6. Extended Model Evaluation\n    # ==========================================================\n    \n    # Training Accuracy\n    y_pred_train = model.predict(X_train)\n    train_acc = accuracy_score(y_train, y_pred_train)\n    print(f\"✅ Training Accuracy: {train_acc:.4f}\")\n\n    # Test Accuracy\n    y_pred = model.predict(X_test)\n    test_acc = accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred)\n    print(f\"✅ Test Accuracy: {test_acc:.4f}\")\n\n    # Classification Report\n    print(\"\\nClassification Report:\")\n    print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred, digits=3))\n\n    # Confusion Matrix\n    cm = confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred)\n    plt.figure(figsize=(10,8))\n    sns.heatmap(cm, annot=True, fmt='d', cmap='Blues')\n    plt.xlabel(\"Predicted\")\n    plt.ylabel(\"Actual\")\n    plt.title(\"Confusion Matrix\")\n    plt.show()\n\n    # Precision / Recall / F1 (Macro & Weighted)\n    print(\"Precision (Macro):\", precision_score(y_test, y_pred, average='macro'))\n    print(\"Recall (Macro):\", recall_score(y_test, y_pred, average='macro'))\n    print(\"F1-score (Macro):\", f1_score(y_test, y_pred, average='macro'))\n    print(\"Precision (Weighted):\", precision_score(y_test, y_pred, average='weighted'))\n    print(\"Recall (Weighted):\", recall_score(y_test, y_pred, average='weighted'))\n    print(\"F1-score (Weighted):\", f1_score(y_test, y_pred, average='weighted'))\n\n    # Matthews Correlation Coefficient & Cohen's Kappa\n    print(\"Matthews Correlation Coefficient (MCC):\", matthews_corrcoef(y_test, y_pred))\n    print(\"Cohen Kappa Score:\", cohen_kappa_score(y_test, y_pred))\n\n    # Log Loss\n    y_proba = model.predict_proba(X_test)\n    print(\"Log Loss:\", log_loss(y_test, y_proba))\n\n    # ROC-AUC (Multi-class)\n    n_classes = len(np.unique(y_test))\n    y_test_bin = label_binarize(y_test, classes=range(n_classes))\n    roc_auc_macro = roc_auc_score(y_test_bin, y_proba, average=\"macro\", multi_class=\"ovr\")\n    roc_auc_weighted = roc_auc_score(y_test_bin, y_proba, average=\"weighted\", multi_class=\"ovr\")\n    print(\"ROC-AUC (Macro):\", roc_auc_macro)\n    print(\"ROC-AUC (Weighted):\", roc_auc_weighted)\n\n    # ROC Curves (One-vs-Rest)\n    plt.figure(figsize=(8,6))\n    for i in range(n_classes):\n        fpr, tpr, _ = roc_curve(y_test_bin[:, i], y_proba[:, i])\n        plt.plot(fpr, tpr, label=f\"Class {i} (AUC={auc(fpr, tpr):.2f})\")\n    plt.plot([0,1], [0,1], 'k--')  # Random performance line\n    plt.xlabel(\"False Positive Rate\")\n    plt.ylabel(\"True Positive Rate\")\n    plt.title(\"ROC Curves (Multi-Class)\")\n    plt.legend()\n    plt.show()\n\n# ==========================================================\n# 🔹 EXECUTION\n# ==========================================================\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-01-02T20:20:31.472895Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-01-02T20:20:31.473190Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-01-02T20:25:35.138830Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-01-02T20:20:31.473167Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-01-02T20:25:35.138219Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Total candidates: 546\n","output_type":"stream"},{"name":"stderr","text":"Loading embeddings: 100%|██████████| 546/546 [04:28<00:00,  2.03it/s]\n","output_type":"stream"},{"name":"stdout","text":"✅ Loaded embeddings for 512/546 candidates\n0:\tlearn: 1.0925485\ttotal: 76.7ms\tremaining: 38.3s\n100:\tlearn: 0.7605354\ttotal: 6.84s\tremaining: 27s\n200:\tlearn: 0.6372228\ttotal: 13.5s\tremaining: 20s\n300:\tlearn: 0.5521451\ttotal: 19.9s\tremaining: 13.1s\n400:\tlearn: 0.4578322\ttotal: 26.3s\tremaining: 6.5s\n499:\tlearn: 0.3866216\ttotal: 32.8s\tremaining: 0us\n✅ Model training completed successfully!\n✅ Training Accuracy: 0.9173\n✅ Test Accuracy: 0.9029\n\nClassification Report:\n              precision    recall  f1-score   support\n\n           0      0.929     0.963     0.945        27\n           1      0.933     0.894     0.913        47\n           2      0.833     0.862     0.847        29\n\n    accuracy                          0.903       103\n   macro avg      0.898     0.906     0.902       103\nweighted avg      0.904     0.903     0.903       103\n\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1000x800 with 2 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"Precision (Macro): 0.8984126984126984\nRecall (Macro): 0.9062163165856001\nF1-score (Macro): 0.9019852169446864\nPrecision (Weighted): 0.9039297272306982\nRecall